        "procedure": "DyCl3·6H2O (0.1 mmol, 37.6 mg) and H4L (0.1 mmol, 40.3 mg) were added to a mixture of 10 mL MeOH and 5 mL MeCN under stirring in an ice bath. When the mixture was clear, Et3N (0.2 mmol, 28 μL) was added under stirring. The mixture was stirred for 1 h, filtered and slowly volatilized at temperature below 293 K. Pale-yellow block crystals suitable for X-ray diffraction were obtained after 3 days.",
